#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Job state for the factory: the only writer of .factory/jobs/<id>/job.json.

The orchestrator never edits job.json itself. This script applies the state machine
(stages, rounds and their budget, verdicts, REWORK, resumes, the queue and capacity) under
a lock, from the files the agents wrote, and prints what to do next. The first line of
the output is always one of:

  ACTION: <what>   do it, then run `.factory/job next <id>` (or the THEN: line)
  WAIT: <reason>   nothing to do now (queued: no capacity)
  DONE: <stage>    the job is at rest (needs-human, merged, pushed, pr-open, superseded)
  ERROR: <reason>  bad request; nothing changed (exit 2)

Later lines: details (AGENT/MODEL/PROMPT blocks for spawns), then NOTE: and STARTED: lines
(a queued job that just got a slot: run `job next` for it too).

  job new "<feature>" [--mode full|light|docs] [--issue N --issue-url URL]... [--untrusted]
          [--delivery local|push|pr]   (this job only; default config.delivery.mode)
          (--issue may be repeated: one job for a bundle of small related issues)
  job triage prepare <raw-issues.json> [--no-agent]   filter the forge's open issues, then spawn factory-triage
  job triage bundle <docs|light|full> <nr>...   one job for issues you chose yourself (after prepare);
                                      a bundle issue (label factory:bundle) on its own: it and its members
  job triage plan                     validate the triage plan, print the groups (jobs to start)
  job triage start <k>                start group k of the plan as a job
  job next <id> [--respawn]           apply what is due, print the next action. An agent whose file is
                                      missing and that was spawned less than limits.respawn_after_min
                                      (default 45) ago counts as still running: WAIT, no resume spent;
                                      --respawn = it has returned without its file, spawn it again
  job reviewers <id> <a,b,c>          record round N's reviewer candidates: kept only when the diff
                                      touches their paths (config.reviewer_paths; code and audit always),
                                      round > 1 narrowed by .factory/rereview; then as `next`
  job delivered <id> merged|pushed|pr-open [--pr-url URL]
  job pr-merged <id>                  the forge confirmed the PR/MR is merged
  job approve <id>                    a human approves a needs-human job: deliver it
  job rework <id> [--untrusted] "<note>"
  job sync <id>                       start (or continue) a base merge of a pr-open job (needs no job slot:
                                      at most limits.active_syncs, default 2, at once)
  job sync-done <id>                  the synced branch is pushed
  job adopt <pr|mr nr>                adopt an open PR/MR made outside the factory (allowed author, same
                                      repo): a minimal pr-open job on its own branch, only so its merge
                                      conflicts can be patched (job sync: merge, targeted tests, push)
  job adoptable                       open PRs/MRs by allowed authors with a merge conflict and no job
                                      (config adopt_conflicting: true adopts them)
  job requeue <id> ["<reason>"]       put a queued job, or one at spec before round 1, at the end of the queue
                                      (state kept: spec.md, acceptance tests, worktree); frees its slot
  job prs [<id>]                      ask the forge about every pr-open job: merged -> merged + close-issues;
                                      conflict or behind the base -> ACTION: sync (syncs go before new jobs)
  job close-issues <id>               after a merge: close the job's issues the forge left open ("Fixed in
                                      !N (<sha>)"); a partial issue (Refs #N, left: ...) stays open, reported
  job fail <id> "<reason>"            -> needs-human
  job drop <id> ["<reason>"]          clear a needs-human or queued job that is not wanted any more:
                                      -> superseded, worktree and unpushed branch removed (refuses a job with an open PR/MR)
  job set <id> pr_url|pr_state|issue_closed|issues|ui_review <json or text>   (issues: a JSON list, for a bundle
                                      made by hand; ui_review: light|full|auto, the ux/ui review form of this job)
  job show <id> [--json]              read-only: stage, round and the pending action (--json: job.json)
  job list | capacity
  job pause ["<reason>"]              start no queued job (the queue holds; new jobs only queue); running
                                      jobs, syncs, adopt and delivery go on. State: .factory/paused
  job unpause                         end the pause and start queued jobs while there is room
  job report [--json]                 from metrics.jsonl: per role runs, first-pass yield, median
                                      duration, verdict mix; per job mode the agent runs per job
"""
